WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.451
Connecting a cloud app to your directory

2
00:00:02.451 --> 00:00:05.063
can quietly move data
outside your boundary.

3
00:00:05.063 --> 00:00:09.937
In the government cloud most agencies use,
nothing in the app gallery is marked.

4
00:00:09.937 --> 00:00:13.249
CISA's directive requires
that only administrators

5
00:00:13.249 --> 00:00:16.413
can approve app access, and
the program applies that.

6
00:00:16.413 --> 00:00:18.676
But that rule decides who approves.

7
00:00:18.676 --> 00:00:21.131
It says nothing about
whether the service on

8
00:00:21.131 --> 00:00:23.787
the other end is authorized
to hold federal data.

9
00:00:23.787 --> 00:00:29.001
A tenant can pass every consent check and
still send data to an uncertified service.

10
00:00:29.001 --> 00:00:31.053
Only an authorization verdict,

11
00:00:31.053 --> 00:00:34.763
recorded before anything is
configured, closes that gap.

12
00:00:34.763 --> 00:00:39.037
The decision for the identity governance
officer: record each service's

13
00:00:39.037 --> 00:00:42.813
authorization status first, and
stop the request if it's missing.

14
00:00:42.813 --> 00:00:44.590
Next, the inventory.
